## Root Cause
The use of user-supplied values directly in the database query can allow an attacker to manipulate the SQL query via injection.

## Explanation
The patch implements a parameterized query by using the Sequelize ORM's built-in functionality, helping to ensure that user input is safely escaped and cannot alter the intended SQL command. This reduces the risk of SQL injection by separating the query structure from its data.

